    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 949 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking strong thunderstorms along a line extending from 3 miles northwest of Fremont to 3 miles northeast of Davey to 4 miles southwest of Pioneers Park. Movement was southeast at 45 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is possible. * Locations impacted include... Omaha, Lincoln, southwestern Council Bluffs, Bellevue, Papillion, Ralston, Wahoo, Gretna, Boys Town, Elkhorn, Millard, Offutt AFB, La Vista, Plattsmouth, Carter Lake, Waverly, Ashland, Syracuse, Springfield, and Yutan. People attending Saunders County Fairgrounds should seek safe shelter immediately! This includes the following highways... Interstate 80 in Iowa near mile marker 1. Interstate 80 in Nebraska between mile markers 388 and 454.",
